# Sprint 3 Execution Log

I ran the server and two clients in three terminals on localhost. Below is what each terminal printed.

What happens in this run:

- Both clients connect at the same time, each on its own handler thread (`Handler-1` and `Handler-2` in the server log).
- Client 2 tries the name PowderDay, which is taken, and picks BassDrop instead.
- BassDrop tries to move first and gets `OUT_OF_TURN`. Later PowderDay tries column 9 and gets `COLUMN_OUT_OF_RANGE`. Neither changes the board.
- 7 moves are played and PowderDay wins with four in a row in column 3. Both players get `GAME_OVER` with the score.
- Round 2 starts on its own. After one move BassDrop types `q`, so PowderDay wins by forfeit and goes back to the lobby.
- The server prints each FSM transition number (T1-T16) and shuts down with Ctrl+C at the end.

